      "pronunciationText": "Here's last video's plan in a savings app, a digital tool like a spreadsheet or a financial calculator. Three hundred dollars a month, at four point eight per cent a year, compounded monthly, for five years, gives twenty thousand, two hundred and ninety-eight dollars and five cents. You can change four things: the deposit, the rate, the number of years, or some money in the account at the start. Which change makes the biggest difference? Make a guess."
