      "pronunciationText": "First, with no starting balance, double the deposit to six hundred dollars a month. The future value becomes forty thousand, five hundred and ninety-six dollars and eleven cents, exactly double, to within a cent. Here's why. Every term in the sum has the deposit as a factor. Double the deposit, and every term doubles, so the total doubles. The interest doubles too, so it's still the same share of the total."
