      "pronunciationText": "The future value doubles, exactly. In the formula, M multiplies everything, and r and n haven't changed. For example, two hundred dollars a month gives thirty-two thousand, seven hundred and seventy-five dollars eighty-seven, and four hundred gives twice that. Saying it more than doubles is the classic mistake. Each deposit still grows for the same time, at the same rate."
